This project explores and analyzes IPL (Indian Premier League) player data to uncover patterns in performance, salary distribution, team strategies, and more. Built using Python in Jupyter Notebook, the analysis focuses on delivering insights through clean code, visualizations, and interpretation.

📌 Objective

To analyze IPL player statistics and team compositions to answer questions like:
Who are the top-performing players by runs/wickets?
How are salaries distributed across teams?
What traits define consistent players?
Which teams are more batting or bowling-heavy?

📁 File Details

Predictive Analytics (IPL Players).ipynb – Jupyter Notebook containing the entire analysis with visuals, summary stats, and observations

📊 Key Areas Covered

Data Loading
IPL dataset loaded using pandas
Initial inspection of rows, columns, and structure
Data Cleaning
Handled missing values, renamed columns for clarity
Converted datatypes where necessary
Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
Top run scorers, wicket-takers
Player-wise and team-wise salary analysis
Distribution of player roles (batsman, bowler, all-rounder)
Age, nationality, experience breakdowns

Visualizations

Bar charts, pie charts, histograms, and heatmaps using matplotlib and seaborn
Trend comparisons across teams and seasons (if available)
Insights & Takeaways
Who gives more value per rupee paid
Over-represented or underused players
Team-building strategies and biases

🛠 Tech Stack

Python 3
Jupyter Notebook
Pandas
NumPy
Matplotlib
Seaborn

✅ How to Run

Download or clone this repository
Open Predictive Analytics (IPL Players).ipynb in Jupyter Notebook or VS Code

Install dependencies:

bash
Copy
Edit
pip install pandas matplotlib seaborn
Run the notebook cell by cell

